Product of USRT97r#2764rt1. Heat oven to 425 degrees. Remove
.  side muscle; use for stew. Remove
.  fat and silver membrane.
2. Fold thin end under. Rub roast
.  with softened butter and season.
.  Place on a rack in a shallow pan.
3. Roast until internal temp reaches
.  135 deg for MedRare (13min/lb if
.  2-3 lb, or 10 min/lb if 4-5 lb).
4. Let stand 10 min. before carving.
OPTIONS: Indirect Grill, Rotisserie
Product of USRT97r#2765rt1. Season or marinate up 24 hours.
2. Heat charcoal 30 min. Heat gas
a .  grill 10 min. with LiD CLosed.
3. Grill 4'' above Medium heat.
.  Hold palm just above grate. If
.  heat causes you to pull away in 4
.  seconds, heat is ideal (375 deg).
4. Cook 10 minutes per side.
5. Slice across grain. Serve in
.  tortillas w/ grilled onions
.  and pico de gallo.
Product of USRT97r#2766rt--COOKING STEPS--
1. Heat oven to 425 degrees.
2. Season roast with a blend of soft
.  butter, salt and pepper. Place on
.  a rack in a shallow roasting pan.
3. Roast, uncovered, until a meat
.  thermometer inserted in center,
.  reads 135 degrees for Medium Rare
.  (13-15 min/lb if 2 to 3 lb).
4. Let stand 10 min. before carving.
OPTIONS: Indirect Grill, Rotisserie
Product of USRT97r#2767rt1. Optional: tenderize each side of
.  meat 2 times with a Jaccard.
2. Marinate 6-24 hours in an acidic
