meat thermometer inserted sideways
to be sure patties reach internal
temperature of 160 deg throughout.
Product of US, MEXICORT97r#2866rt1. Marinate meat 20 min. or season.
2. Heat a wok or large heavy skillet
.  over High heat 3 min. Add 1 Tbsp.
.  oil to wok and tip pan to coat.
3. Cook 1/2 to 3/4 pound at a time
.  to preventcrowding. Stir fry
.  1 to 2 min., scooping and turning
.  continuously, until no longer
.  pink. Do not over cook.
4. Remove meat and cook vegetables.
.  Then combine and heat through.
Product of US, MEXICORT97r#2868rt1. Before cooking or marinating, cut
.  a thin slice from each end to
.  expose meat and allow skin to be
.  removed after grilling. Optional:
.  Season or marinate up to 24 hrs.
2. Grill over Mediumheat (375
.  degree surface temp is ideal).
3. Cook with skin on 10 min./side.
4. Peel skin from meat. Slice across
.  grain. Season. Serve in tortillas
.  w/ grilled onions & pico de gallo.
Product of US, MEXICORT97r#2869rt----------COOKING STEPS------------
1. Marinate steak 2 to 6 hours in an
.  acidic marinade in refrigerator
.  or season as desired.
2. Grill 4 inches above Medium heat.
.  Hold palm just above grate. If
.  heat causes you to pull away in 4
.  seconds, heat is ideal (375 deg).
3. Cook on open grill 3-8 min/side
.  depending on thickness. Slice
.  thinly across grain. OPTION:Broil
