.   Cook to 155 deg internal temp.
OPTIONS: Bake/Roast,Broil,Pan BroilRT97r#8181rt------------COOKING STEPS-----------
1. Dust roast with seasoned flour.
2. Brown each side in 2 Tbsp. heated
.  oil over Medium heat in a stock
.  pot. Wipe or drain oil from pot.
3. Add 1/2 cup beefbroth or 1 can
.  diced tomatoes to pot. Season.
4. Cover and simmer gently over Low
.  heat 2 1/2-3 hours until tender.
.  Do not boil or meat will toughen.
5. Add vegetables during last hour.
OPTIONS: Stew, Cut into Cubes & StewRT97r#8182rt------------COOKING STEPS-----------
1. Dust roast with seasoned flour.
2. Brown each side in 2 Tbsp. heated
.  oil over Medium heat in a stock
.  pot. Wipe or drain oil from pot.
3. Add 1/2 cup beefbroth or 1 can
.  diced tomatoes to pot. Season.
4. Cover and simmer gently over Low
.  heat 2 to 3 hours until tender.
.  Do not boil or meat will toughen.
5. Add vegetables during last hour.
OPTIONS: Stew, Cut into Cubes & StewRT97r#8183rt------------COOKING STEPS-----------
1. Heat oven to 325 degrees. Press
.  seasonings onto surface of roast.
2. Place on a rack in a shallow
.  roasting pan. Do not add water.
3. Roast, uncovered, incenter of
.  oven 35 minutes per pound or
.  until a meat thermometer inserted
.  in the center reads 135 degrees.
4. Let stand 15 minutes before
.  slicing thinly across the grain.
OPTIONS:Indirect Grill, Braise, StewRT97r#8184rt------------COOKING STEPS-----------
1. Dust roast with seasoned flour.
2. Brown all sides in 2 Tbsp. heated
.  oil over Medium heat in a stock
.  pot. Wipe or drain oil from pot.
3. Add enough beef broth, water and
.  1 can diced tomatoes (optional)
.  to just cover roast. Season.
4. Cover and simmer gently over Low
.  heat 3 hours until fork tender.
.  Do not boil or meat will toughen.
OPTIONS:Braise,Cut into Cubes & StewRT97r#8185rt------------COOKING STEPS-----------
1. Heat oven to 325 degrees. Press
.  seasonings onto surface of roast.
2. Place on a rack in a shallow
.  roasting pan. Do not add water.
3. Roast, uncovered, incenter of
.  oven 30 to 35 min per pound or
.  until a meat thermometer inserted
.  in the center reads 140 degrees.
4. Let stand 15 min. before slicing
.  thinly across the grain.
OPTIONS:Indirect Grill, Braise, StewRT97r#8186rt------------COOKING STEPS-----------
1. Heat oven to 325 degrees. Press
.  seasonings onto surface of roast.
2. Place on a rack in a shallow
.  roasting pan. Do not add water.
3. Roast, uncovered, incenter of
.  oven 25 to 30 min per pound or
.  until a meat thermometer inserted
.  in the center reads 135 degrees.
4. Let stand 15 min. before slicing
.  thinly across the grain.
OPTIONS: Braise, StewRT97r#9783rt----------COOKING STEPS------------
1. Cut skirts into 10-inch sections.
2. Optional: tenderize w/ a Jaccard.
3. Marinate 6-24 hours in an acidic
.  marinade in the refrigerator.
4. Grill over Medium-Hot heat (425
.  degree surface temp is ideal).
5. Cook on an open grill 5 to 8 min.
.  per side depending on thickness.
.  Slice thinly across grain with
.  knife held at a 45 degree angle.
OPTIONS: Broil, Pan Fry, Pan BroilRT97r#9895rt----COOKING STEPS-INDIRECT GRILL----
1. Arrange charcoal in half of grill
.  and heat 30 min. or heat one side
.  of gas grill 10 min-lid closed.
2. Sear steaks directly over heat 3
.  min/side then move to cool side.
3. Cook 25-35 min in a closed grill
.  (35-40 min if 2" thick). Keep air
.  temp in chamber at 350-400 deg.
4. Remove steak at 135 deg internal
.  temp (MedRare). Let stand 10 min.
OPTION: Sear & Roast-400 deg ovenRT97r#9896rt----COOKING STEPS-INDIRECT GRILL----
1. Arrange charcoal in half of grill
